OL,3,GNEWSACall for all schools to get
OL,4,Aepilepsy training
OL,5,
OL,6,F"It was terrifying," said Lyndsey,
OL,7,Frecalling her five-year-old daughter
OL,8,FGrace's first seizure that was followed
OL,9,Fby others and led to an epilepsy
OL,10,Fdiagnosis.
OL,12,FAs Grace learnt to live with the
OL,13,Fneurological condition, Lyndsey said
OL,14,Fthe prospect of how it may impact her
OL,15,Fschool life in Par, Cornwall, was
OL,16,Fdaunting.
OL,18,FBut Lyndsey's fears were allayed when
OL,19,Fthe school said it would train all its
OL,20,Fteachers to respond to seizures and
OL,21,Fdispense emergency medication.
OL,23,APub: 19-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBW-SW Eng NewsC Reg TVFWeather
